# Weekly reports (reports/) and the decisions database (data/fpl_automate.db)
# are INTENTIONALLY tracked in git -- they are this project's audit trail of
# what was recommended and (once recorded) whether it worked. Only the raw
# HTTP response cache is disposable.
data/cache/

# Raw historical per-season archive (ml/historical.py) used to train the ML
# model -- large (tens of MB across seasons) and fully regenerable from
# vaastav/Fantasy-Premier-League, so it's disposable like data/cache/.
# models/*.joblib and models/ml_calibration.json are the OPPOSITE: small
# (~3.5MB total), deterministic given fixed seeds + data, and needed by
# weekly-plan.yml without retraining twice a day -- INTENTIONALLY tracked,
# same reasoning as reports/ above.
data/historical/

